L0229: Definition conversion lacks a valid target

fold! or unfold! needs an appropriate checked definition and, when closing evidence, an expected claim. The selector must name the definition involved; a model selector must correspond to an available observation. Supply an explicit result annotation and the correct definition.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/fold_without_claim.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// `fold!` with nothing to say which claim it should produce.
#[terminates] #[no_panic] #[no_io] logic fn nonzero(x: Int) -> Prop { prop!(x != 0) }

#[terminates] #[no_panic] #[no_io] fn first(n: u8, h: @(n != 0)) -> @nonzero(n) {
    let folded = fold!(nonzero, h);
    folded
}
```

Language, as built: [1.7:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.7:1).
